    {
      "sourceId": "src-80dcd4f61601ef01",
      "quote": "Research Focus Our lab focuses on understanding the placenta affected pregnancy complications. We use pluripotent stem cells to model the placenta in disease and study the pathophysiology of pregnancy complications at the molecular and cellular level. We are currently studying a variety of diseases such as preeclampsia, complete hydatidiform mole, and Trisomy 21. Lab News & Highlights ​ https://blog.cirm.ca.gov/tag/mariko-horii/ Maddie got into grad school and will be joining University of Virginia Summer of 2022. Congrats Maddie! Tony got into Master's program and will be joining Cal Poly SLO Summer of 2023. Congrats Tony! Contact Us We are located at the Sanford Consortium for Regenerative Medicine. Contact Dr. Horii if you are interested in the lab: Mariko Horii mhorii@health.ucsd.edu",
